<Sequential id="SequentialAdaptiveDemo" title="Adaptive Sequence">
  <CapaProblem id="seq_check" title="Concept Check">
    How many sides does a hexagon have?
    <NumericalGrader id="seq_grader" answer="6" tolerance="0">
      <NumberInput id="seq_answer" placeholder="Enter a number" />
    </NumericalGrader>
  </CapaProblem>

  <Markdown id="scaffold_review" title="Review" when="@seq_check.correct === correctness.incorrect">
### Let's review

The prefix *hex-* means six. Think of other hex- words:
- **Hexadecimal** — base-16 (but the prefix still means six!)
- **Hexapod** — six-legged creature (insects)
  </Markdown>

  <CapaProblem id="seq_retry" title="Try Again" when="@seq_check.correct === correctness.incorrect">
    Now that you've reviewed: how many sides does a hexagon have?
    <NumericalGrader id="seq_retry_grader" answer="6" tolerance="0">
      <NumberInput id="seq_retry_answer" placeholder="Enter a number" />
    </NumericalGrader>
  </CapaProblem>

  <Markdown id="seq_summary" title="Summary">
A hexagon has **6 sides**. The prefix *hex-* is from Greek, meaning six.
  </Markdown>
</Sequential>
